{"accepted_at":"2026-08-30T14:53:58.032964Z","case":{"argument_date":"2025-11-05T00:00:00Z","arguments":[{"argument_date":"2025-11-05T00:00:00Z","heading":"What happened at the argument","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2025","official_transcript_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","paragraphs":["General Sauer argued the President declared a national emergency over trade deficits and fentanyl. That declaration authorizes the tariffs.","Mr. Katyal argued tariffs are taxes. The taxing power belongs to Congress alone. The President has no Article II tariff authority.","Justice Sotomayor questioned whether tariffs are taxes. She also asked if any foreign-facing emergency could justify them.","Chief Justice Roberts questioned the reliance on Dames & Moore. He noted the Court called that decision narrow."],"reargument":false,"sequence":1,"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 11, lines 31-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 11, lines 31-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 13, lines 35-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 13, lines 35-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 135, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 135, lines 19-11"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 136, lines 15-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 136, lines 15-17"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label"