_at":"2026-08-29T20:06:14.219551Z","explanation":"An official oral-argument transcript was verified.","status":"argued"},{"changed_at":"2026-08-29T23:55:39.455383Z","explanation":"An official Court opinion was verified.","status":"decided"}],"case_status":"decided","dek":"The dispute is whether the President may impose tariffs without congressional approval. One side calls them taxes reserved to Congress. The other calls them emergency regulatory tools.","dek_sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 135, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 135, lines 19-11"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 160, lines 55-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 160, lines 55-47"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 186, lines 47-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 186, lines 47-17"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 25-29","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 25-29"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 69, lines 27-29","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 69, lines 27-29"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 98, lines 37-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 98, lines 37-47"}],"maturity":"post_opinion","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2025","official_disposition_urls":["https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/607us2r12_8nj9.pdf"],"official_docket_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/docket/docketfiles/html/public/24-1287.html","primary_docket":"24-1287","revisions":[{"correction_note":"Rewritten to the concise citizen-facing editorial standard.","created_at":"2026-08-30T14:53:58.032964Z","maturity":"post_opinion","revision_number":1}],"schema_version":"1.0","sections":[{"heading":"What this case is about","paragraphs":["The federal parties want the tariffs upheld as a valid emergency power. The opposing side wants the tariffs struck down as an unconstitutional tax."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 135, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 135, lines 19-11"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 160, lines 55-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 160, lines 55-47"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 186, lines 47-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 186, lines 47-17"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 25-29","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 25-29"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 69, lines 27-29","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 69, lines 27-29"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 98, lines 37-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 98, lines 37-47"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on November 5, 2025."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 138, lines 21-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 138, lines 21-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 11-23","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 11-23"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 74, lines 35-39","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 74, lines 35-39"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["The federal parties want the tariffs upheld as a valid emergency power.","The opposing side wants the tariffs struck down as an unconstitutional tax."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 135, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 135, lines 19-11"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 160, lines 55-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 160, lines 55-47"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 186, lines 47-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 186, lines 47-17"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 5, lines 25-29","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 5, lines 25-29"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 69, lines 27-29","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 69, lines 27-29"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 98, lines 37-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 98, lines 37-47"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["The President declared a national emergency over trade deficits and fentanyl trafficking. That declaration justifies the tariffs under emergency powers.","Tariffs are taxes. The Constitution gives the taxing power to Congress alone. The President bypassed Congress and imposed a major tax increase."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 135, lines 19-11","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 135, lines 19-11"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 160, lines 55-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 160, lines 55-47"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 186, lines 47-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2025/24-1287_b07d.pdf","page_label":"file page 186, lines 47-17"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcrip